The Fieldglass crates themselves (`fieldglass`, `fieldglass-core`,
`fieldglass-grib1`, `fieldglass-grib2`, `fieldglass-netcdf`, `fieldglass-zarr`,
`fieldglass-aec`, which decodes GRIB2 section 5.42 CCSDS / AEC packing, and
`fieldglass-napi`) are part of this project and carry the same MIT OR
Apache-2.0 terms as the package.

This list is generated from the addon's own dependency graph
(`cargo tree -p fieldglass-napi --target all -e normal,no-proc-macro`) and is
regenerated when that graph changes. A test holds it to the graph. `cargo deny
check` holds the whole workspace to an allowed-license set on every pull
request, so a crate whose terms this project cannot ship never reaches a
release.

